==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Snache]]s (4,000%) spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Snache]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns.
**5 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Dober P.D]] spawns.
**1 [[Croakley]] spawns.

==Strategy==
If you let a very small army hit the base, with no line of meatshields behind, you'll be able to let them die. Then, you can do most of the fight with R.Ost without interferences, then deal with the others to make the stage much easier. Wave blockers are recommended: you should let them get slowed, so they'll last longer and protect the backlines.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]], [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Wall Cat]] - Both Anti-Traitless meatshields, so you can let them soak up all the damage in this stage. Just beware that Haniwa is very prone to being perpetually slowed by Croakley.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - A great asset on later replays, and even has [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] to dismiss Dober P.D.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] - If you have him by this point, you can just let him out and he'll deal great damage to everything. Like Haniwa, Jagando is also prone to getting slowed, so try to time him well.
*Any [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless]] Uber - As long as they outrange R.Ost or can deal damage fast enough, they'll do great in this stage.

